From 8618667f7f25f52e443ffbab3cb3c484b3f206ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 10:08:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] soc/integration: add basic checks to
 SoCCSRHandler.add_region

The CSR-side add_region was a 1-line dict-set with a long-standing
`# FIXME: add checks` comment. Add the three checks that catch
real out-of-tree mistakes without restricting any reasonable use:

  - Type check: region must be a SoCCSRRegion. Catches transposed
    arguments or misuse of the bus-side SoCRegion class.
  - Duplicate name: a CSR region added twice raises SoCError
    (matches the existing behavior of SoCBusHandler.add_region).
  - Origin alignment: the origin must land on a paging boundary
    (origin % csr.paging == 0). The standard csr_bankarray flow
    always satisfies this; the check fires on hand-rolled CSR
    regions whose origin is computed wrong.

Overlap is *not* checked here: by construction the in-tree CSR
allocation flow (csr.address_map -> SoCLocHandler.alloc) hands
out distinct slots, so two regions can't legitimately collide.

Verified: built 6 diverse litex-boards targets end-to-end with
--no-compile-software --no-compile-gateware:

  digilent_arty            778263 B
  sipeed_tang_nano_20k     331701 B
  terasic_de10nano          97760 B
  alchitry_au              775263 B
  terasic_de2_115          338874 B
  berkeleylab_marble      1356632 B

All exit 0, all produce gateware. test_wishbone.py 23/23.
Three negative-path unit checks confirm each new check raises
SoCError on bad input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 litex/soc/integration/soc.py | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/litex/soc/integration/soc.py b/litex/soc/integration/soc.py
index aea0284ef..bef9533df 100644
--- a/litex/soc/integration/soc.py
+++ b/litex/soc/integration/soc.py
@@ -871,7 +871,26 @@ class SoCCSRHandler(SoCLocHandler):
 
     # Add Region -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     def add_region(self, name, region):
-        # FIXME: add checks
+        # Type check.
+        if not isinstance(region, SoCCSRRegion):
+            self.logger.error("{} is not a {}.".format(
+                colorer(name, color="red"),
+                colorer("SoCCSRRegion")))
+            raise SoCError()
+        # Duplicate-name check.
+        if name in self.regions:
+            self.logger.error("CSR Region {} {}.".format(
+                colorer(name, color="red"),
+                colorer("already declared")))
+            raise SoCError()
+        # Origin alignment check (origin must land on a paging boundary).
+        if (region.origin % self.paging) != 0:
+            self.logger.error("CSR Region {} origin 0x{:08x} {} CSR paging 0x{:x}.".format(
+                colorer(name, color="red"),
+                region.origin,
+                colorer("not aligned on", color="red"),
+                self.paging))
+            raise SoCError()
         self.regions[name] = region
 
     # Address map ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
